`app/` directory (backend, frontend, scripts, tests). It does NOT cover:

  * Model weights. The fine-tuned SciBETO weights distributed via Google Drive
    inherit the license of the base model Flaglab/SciBETO-large
    (https://huggingface.co/Flaglab/SciBETO-large). The Llama 3.1 8B Instruct
    weights, when downloaded by the application, are subject to the Llama 3.1
    Community License Agreement
    (https://www.llama.com/llama3_1/license/).

  * Datasets. The Gold Test Sets released under `Datos/` are licensed under
    Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0):
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
    Attribution must reference both the Group 2 MAIA 2026 team and the
    associated scientific article (see README §17).

  * Scientific article. The PDF in `docs/Articulo_PLN_Grupo2_2026.pdf` remains
    the academic property of Group 2 and Universidad de los Andes. Cite as
    indicated in README §17.

  * Third-party APIs. Usage of the OpenAI API (GPT-4o-mini) is governed by
    OpenAI's terms of service: https://openai.com/policies/terms-of-use
